# Legacy WordPress URL map (pre-Astro migration).
#
# These paths existed on the old SiteGround-hosted WordPress site and still
# attract inbound links, bookmarks, and ad traffic. Every one of them returned
# a hard 404 after the migration. Each rule sends the old URL to its closest
# live equivalent with a 301 so link equity carries over.
#
# Both the trailing-slash and bare forms are listed: WordPress emitted
# trailing slashes, but inbound links are inconsistent.
#
# Do NOT add rules here for /service-area/horseback-riding, /horse-boarding,
# /ranch-experience, or /san-diego-family-trip — those are real pages now.

